      en: "Brindisi is a port city in Apulia, Italy, on the Adriatic Sea. With about 87,000 inhabitants, it is a major transportation hub. Founded by the Romans in the 2nd century BCE, it was the terminus of the Via Appia. Its natural harbor is shaped like a deer's head (hence the name). Landmarks include the Roman amphitheater, the cathedral, and the Castello Svevo. The port serves ferries to Greece and the Balkans. The city also has an airport.",
